{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8244708",
      "title": "Fetching Meals Data (GET HTTP Request)",
      "sourceHash": "3640e099b63b897eb1313a0cb9d40678aeba398017cef5da1c1792d1b3fd36f4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.64,
          "en": "Now of course adding this header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.64,
          "end": 5.94,
          "en": "was relatively simple and straightforward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.94,
          "end": 9.09,
          "en": "because it's just a very simple component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.09,
          "end": 12.36,
          "en": "Now things are going to get a bit more complex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.36,
          "end": 15.72,
          "en": "because now I want to display my meals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.72,
          "end": 18.48,
          "en": "And for that, I'll add another new component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.48,
          "end": 19.92,
          "en": "in the Components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.92,
          "end": 23.16,
          "en": "which I'll name Meals.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.16,
          "end": 26.55,
          "en": "And the idea here of course is that in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.55,
          "end": 30.75,
          "en": "we load that meal data from that dummy backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.75,
          "end": 34.44,
          "en": "There will have that meals endpoint",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.44,
          "end": 37.05,
          "en": "which handles GET requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.05,
          "end": 39.82,
          "en": "and which then will return us this dummy meal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.785,
          "end": 42.735,
          "en": "data which lives on that dummy backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.83,
          "end": 46.59,
          "en": "So we'll need to send a request to that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.59,
          "end": 48.54,
          "en": "from inside the Meals component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.54,
          "end": 50.973,
          "en": "and then output the meal items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.26,
          "end": 53.94,
          "en": "For that in Meals.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.94,
          "end": 58.83,
          "en": "I'll start by exporting that Meals component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.83,
          "end": 61.983,
          "en": "And then here I'll return an unordered list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.91,
          "end": 65.76,
          "en": "An unordered list with an id of meals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.76,
          "end": 70.23,
          "en": "because again, if you take a look at the index.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.23,
          "end": 72.84,
          "en": "in there you will find such a rule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.84,
          "end": 75.06,
          "en": "that's looking for meals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.06,
          "end": 77.64,
          "en": "and that's indeed intended to be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 80.703,
          "en": "on that list that will display the meals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 85.28999999999999,
          "en": "Now of course, the list alone isn't too helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.28999999999999,
          "end": 88.02,
          "en": "We also need items in that list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.02,
          "end": 91.173,
          "en": "And for that in turn, we need data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.16,
          "end": 95.583,
          "en": "So we need to send such a HTTP request to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.57,
          "end": 97.71000000000001,
          "en": "Now, as I just mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.71000000000001,
          "end": 102.34,
          "en": "we'll need to send a GET request to /meals on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.25999999999999,
          "end": 106.97999999999999,
          "en": "and therefore, we'll need to write some code to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.97999999999999,
          "end": 108.53999999999999,
          "en": "In this course, you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.53999999999999,
          "end": 111.47999999999999,
          "en": "that you can send an HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.47999999999999,
          "end": 113.913,
          "en": "by using the builtin fetch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.81,
          "end": 118.35,
          "en": "This function takes the URL of the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.35,
          "end": 121.08,
          "en": "to which you want to send a request as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.08,
          "end": 125.343,
          "en": "And here that's http://localhost:3000.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.21,
          "end": 128.76,
          "en": "And then it's /meals because again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.76,
          "end": 131.463,
          "en": "that is the endpoint we have to target.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.05,
          "end": 135.21,
          "en": "Now, you could configure this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.21,
          "end": 137.79,
          "en": "and for example change the request method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.79,
          "end": 140.28,
          "en": "but GET is already the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.28,
          "end": 143.7,
          "en": "and we also don't need to send any other information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.7,
          "end": 146.583,
          "en": "and therefore I'll just send a request like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.99,
          "end": 150.6,
          "en": "As you also learned in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.6,
          "end": 153.96,
          "en": "fetch then returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.96,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "and you can use the then method to define a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 161.28,
          "en": "that will be executed when that promise resolves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.28,
          "end": 163.44299999999998,
          "en": "when you gut back a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 167.37,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could use async await,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.37,
          "end": 171.06,
          "en": "but you must not convert your component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.06,
          "end": 174.84300000000002,
          "en": "into a async function because that's not allowed by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 178.68,
          "en": "Therefore, in order to handle this request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.68,
          "end": 183.52,
          "en": "we could use then or wrap this into a separate function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.38,
          "end": 186.5,
          "en": "which we could name fetchMeals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.19,
          "end": 191.19,
          "en": "This can now be an async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.19,
          "end": 193.26,
          "en": "because it's now a standard function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.26,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "inside of the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 198.15,
          "en": "And if we now move that code in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.15,
          "end": 203.15,
          "en": "we can, therefore, use await to get our response like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 206.04,
          "end": 210.54,
          "en": "Now that response then might be an error response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.54,
          "end": 213.09,
          "en": "because maybe the request failed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.09,
          "end": 215.61,
          "en": "maybe something went wrong on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.61,
          "end": 219.72,
          "en": "and therefore, we should check if the response is not OK,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.72,
          "end": 224.4,
          "en": "if it has a 400-ish or 500 ish status code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.4,
          "end": 227.433,
          "en": "in which case we probably should do something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228.48,
          "end": 231.45,
          "en": "And we also probably should do something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.45,
          "end": 234.69,
          "en": "if sending the request fails, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.69,
          "end": 237.27,
          "en": "because there is no internet connection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 237.27,
          "end": 240.423,
          "en": "So we might wanna wrap this with try catch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.04,
          "end": 244.14,
          "en": "Though, we'll do that a little bit later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.14,
          "end": 246.45,
          "en": "because for the moment, I want to keep it simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 246.45,
          "end": 248.34,
          "en": "and just send this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.34,
          "end": 252.003,
          "en": "and expect that we do get back a valid response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.84,
          "end": 256.533,
          "en": "That's also why we'll add this code here later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 257.85,
          "end": 262.53,
          "en": "So to use that data, which we expect to get back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 262.53,
          "end": 266.1,
          "en": "we can and should now call response.json",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 266.1,
          "end": 268.65,
          "en": "because this dummy backend here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 268.65,
          "end": 272.88,
          "en": "will send back its data in JSON format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 272.88,
          "end": 275.7,
          "en": "So using this JSON data format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 275.7,
          "end": 278.94,
          "en": "and therefore, to extract that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 278.94,
          "end": 283.59000000000003,
          "en": "and convert it to JavaScript objects and values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 283.59000000000003,
          "end": 287.97,
          "en": "we must use the JSON method on that response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.97,
          "end": 292.62,
          "en": "And since this also yields a promise as you can see here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 292.62,
          "end": 295.44,
          "en": "we can and should also await this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 295.44,
          "end": 298.51,
          "en": "so that we in the end get back our response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 299.49,
          "end": 302.73,
          "en": "which of course should then be those meals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 302.73,
          "end": 305.67,
          "en": "So we could also name that meals here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 305.67,
          "end": 310.02,
          "en": "because again if we take another look at that dummy backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 310.02,
          "end": 312.75,
          "en": "you see that it's in the end just the meals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 312.75,
          "end": 314.34,
          "en": "loaded from some file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 314.34,
          "end": 317.373,
          "en": "that are being sent back to the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 318.45,
          "end": 320.67,
          "en": "And with that, we'll have our meals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 320.67,
          "end": 325.383,
          "en": "The next step now is to update the UI with that meals data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 326.37,
          "end": 329.4,
          "en": "And of course, since we're awaiting a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 329.4,
          "end": 331.65,
          "en": "and the extraction of the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 331.65,
          "end": 334.44,
          "en": "it makes sense that the meals data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 334.44,
          "end": 336.96,
          "en": "will not be available instantly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 336.96,
          "end": 340.56,
          "en": "when this component function is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 340.56,
          "end": 343.77,
          "en": "Instead, there will very likely be some delay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 343.77,
          "end": 346.74,
          "en": "even if it's just a couple of milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 346.74,
          "end": 349.89,
          "en": "Therefore, the meals will not be there initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 349.89,
          "end": 353.37,
          "en": "and therefore, we should manage them as some state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 353.37,
          "end": 356.19,
          "en": "so that we initially have no meals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 356.19,
          "end": 359.52,
          "en": "and we render a UI without meals data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 359.52,
          "end": 361.83,
          "en": "And then once the meals data arrived,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 361.83,
          "end": 365.073,
          "en": "we update the UI with that new data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 366,
          "end": 369.87,
          "en": "And hence we should use the useState hook here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 369.87,
          "end": 371.29,
          "en": "in this Meals component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 372.18,
          "end": 376.673,
          "en": "and import useState from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 380.08,
          "end": 383.04,
          "en": "And then here, start with an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 383.04,
          "end": 386.76,
          "en": "Since this should be that Meals state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 386.76,
          "end": 390.51,
          "en": "or that loadedMeals state to make it very clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 390.51,
          "end": 394.71,
          "en": "that that meals data will not be there initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 394.71,
          "end": 397.14,
          "en": "Initially it's always this empty array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 397.14,
          "end": 400.71,
          "en": "but then then here in line 13 we'll have the meals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 400.71,
          "end": 403.89,
          "en": "And therefore, after loading those meals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 403.89,
          "end": 407.01,
          "en": "we can update the loadedMeals state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 407.01,
          "end": 411.45,
          "en": "by calling setLoadedMeals to set the loadedMeals equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 411.45,
          "end": 413.763,
          "en": "to the meals we got back from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 416.55,
          "end": 419.34000000000003,
          "en": "And with that, we'll update this state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 419.34000000000003,
          "end": 423.3,
          "en": "and we can now output the meal data down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 423.3,
          "end": 427.14,
          "en": "And for the moment, to keep this relatively simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 427.14,
          "end": 430.08,
          "en": "I'll just use this loadedMeals state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 430.08,
          "end": 433.247,
          "en": "and map every meals item into a list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 433.247,
          "end": 438.04,
          "en": "which gets a key that should be meal.id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 439.05,
          "end": 442.71,
          "en": "because every dummy meal I'm providing on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 442.71,
          "end": 445.98,
          "en": "will have an ID which we can access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 445.98,
          "end": 448.08,
          "en": "And then every meal also has a name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 448.08,
          "end": 450.57,
          "en": "a price, a description and an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 450.57,
          "end": 453.6,
          "en": "And for now I'll just output the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 453.6,
          "end": 455.94,
          "en": "So back here in Meals.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 455.94,
          "end": 458.25,
          "en": "between those list item tags",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 458.25,
          "end": 460.5,
          "en": "I'll output meal.name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 460.5,
          "end": 463.983,
          "en": "just so that we can see whether this works or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 466.32,
          "end": 469.53,
          "en": "Now, at the moment, it'll definitely not work though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 469.53,
          "end": 473.4,
          "en": "because we have all this logic for fetching the meals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 473.4,
          "end": 475.29,
          "en": "and for updating the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 475.29,
          "end": 478.11,
          "en": "inside of this fetchMeals function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 478.11,
          "end": 480.693,
          "en": "which we never call anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 481.53,
          "end": 483.24,
          "en": "And therefore, at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 483.24,
          "end": 485.463,
          "en": "this code will never get executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 486.66,
          "end": 489.48,
          "en": "Now of course we could now call it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 489.48,
          "end": 491.46,
          "en": "in the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 491.46,
          "end": 494.94,
          "en": "but you learned before in this course that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 494.94,
          "end": 497.223,
          "en": "this is not the best idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 498.06,
          "end": 500.31,
          "en": "It's not a great idea because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 500.31,
          "end": 504.09,
          "en": "if we call this function here in the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 504.09,
          "end": 507,
          "en": "obviously this code here will be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 507,
          "end": 510.24,
          "en": "And the problem with that is that in this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 510.24,
          "end": 512.49,
          "en": "we're updating the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 512.49,
          "end": 515.46,
          "en": "Now what happens if you update the state?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 515.46,
          "end": 517.59,
          "en": "Write the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 517.59,
          "end": 521.13,
          "en": "to which this state belongs is executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 521.13,
          "end": 523.95,
          "en": "So therefore, the Meals component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 523.95,
          "end": 525.66,
          "en": "would be executed again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 525.66,
          "end": 529.41,
          "en": "this line of code here would be executed again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 529.41,
          "end": 532.32,
          "en": "and therefore, of course this code would run again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 532.32,
          "end": 534.06,
          "en": "the state would be set again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 534.06,
          "end": 537.3,
          "en": "and we'd end up in an infinite loop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 537.3,
          "end": 539.34,
          "en": "which we definitely don't want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 539.34,
          "end": 542.283,
          "en": "because that would crash our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 543.81,
          "end": 546.87,
          "en": "And that's why for situations like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 546.87,
          "end": 549.03,
          "en": "where we have a side effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 549.03,
          "end": 551.4,
          "en": "that would cause an infinite loop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 551.4,
          "end": 554.04,
          "en": "we should use the useEffect hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 554.04,
          "end": 556.623,
          "en": "about which you also learned earlier in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 557.79,
          "end": 561.54,
          "en": "This hook allows us to run side effects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 561.54,
          "end": 563.28,
          "en": "after the component rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 563.28,
          "end": 567.57,
          "en": "and it also allows us to define a dependencies array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 567.57,
          "end": 569.73,
          "en": "that controls when exactly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 569.73,
          "end": 571.713,
          "en": "the side effect function will run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 572.91,
          "end": 577.68,
          "en": "So, therefore, we can now import useEffect from React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 577.68,
          "end": 581.94,
          "en": "and define this effect function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 581.94,
          "end": 585.54,
          "en": "and then we can move this fetchMeals function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 585.54,
          "end": 587.94,
          "en": "and the call to this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 587.94,
          "end": 589.773,
          "en": "into this effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 591.09,
          "end": 594.12,
          "en": "Now, we could also leave this fetchMeals function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 594.12,
          "end": 596.22,
          "en": "outside of this effect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 596.22,
          "end": 599.64,
          "en": "but then we would have to add it as a dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 599.64,
          "end": 602.34,
          "en": "because we're now using something in the effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 602.34,
          "end": 604.65,
          "en": "That's defined outside of the effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 604.65,
          "end": 608.07,
          "en": "And we then might have to use useCallback here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 608.07,
          "end": 610.08,
          "en": "to avoid that disk changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 610.08,
          "end": 613.2,
          "en": "every time the component function is re-executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 613.2,
          "end": 615.84,
          "en": "And it's just a lot of unnecessary work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 615.84,
          "end": 618.66,
          "en": "since this fetchMeals function is only used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 618.66,
          "end": 620.643,
          "en": "in this effect function anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 621.6,
          "end": 624,
          "en": "So moving it into this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 624,
          "end": 626.373,
          "en": "is the simplest way of dealing with this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 627.57,
          "end": 632.16,
          "en": "And therefore, now we also execute this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 632.16,
          "end": 634.98,
          "en": "after the component function executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 634.98,
          "end": 637.86,
          "en": "But if we got no dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 637.86,
          "end": 640.92,
          "en": "or if we got dependencies that never change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 640.92,
          "end": 643.44,
          "en": "this code will never execute again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 643.44,
          "end": 646.143,
          "en": "and therefore, we won't have an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 648.09,
          "end": 652.59,
          "en": "Now indeed here, we don't have to add any dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 652.59,
          "end": 655.02,
          "en": "because this effect function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 655.02,
          "end": 659.76,
          "en": "is now not using any external props or state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 659.76,
          "end": 664.76,
          "en": "or any other values that could change across renders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 665.16,
          "end": 668.55,
          "en": "The only external thing it's using,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
